//? Title: Jackknife: Actual Deletions, Bias Identities and Median Limits
//? Subtitle: Complete and sampled delete-d experiments on tiny data and iris Sepal.Length
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Estimate the bias and sampling uncertainty of a statistic by seeing how it
changes when observations are systematically omitted. The jackknife turns actual
deletion statistics into pseudo-values and a scaled variance estimate. We first
check the algebra on three observations and enumerate a tiny delete-two example,
then preserve the original iris variance, mean and median experiments. Exact
identities for smooth statistics are separated from rounded-median pathologies,
conditional Monte Carlo error and assumptions needed for inference. Neither a
larger deletion count nor agreement with one bootstrap run certifies an
uncertainty estimate.
)
\toc

> Three observations and an actual deletion

For [1,2,4], the mean is seven thirds. Deleting the final observation leaves
[1,2] and mean 1.5. Its pseudo-value is three times seven thirds minus twice
1.5, or four: the original observation. The next program evaluates the statistic
once on the full sample and once per deletion. The diagram reads those actual
results; pseudo-values are algebraic transforms, not independent new data.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/jackknife_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/jackknife_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/bootstrap.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <algorithm>
#include <format>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const std::vector<double> x{1, 2, 4};
    const auto f =
        dm::stats::jackknife_statistic(dm::stats::JackknifeStatistic::Mean);
    const auto r = dm::stats::jackknife_checked(x, f);
    std::print("| deleted index | original value | actual leave-one-out mean | pseudo-value |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < x.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {:.0f} | {:.8f} | {:.8f} |\n", i, x[i],
                   r.leave_one_out[i], r.pseudo_values[i]);
    std::print("Full mean {:.8f}, bias {:.8e}, corrected {:.8f}, SE {:.8f}.\n",
               r.estimate, r.bias, r.bias_corrected, r.standard_error);
    dm::stats::jackknife_deletion_diagram(x, r, 2).save_svg(
        "build/jackknife_tiny.svg");
}
```
