> Why the rounded median has zero delete-one spread

For an even sample of 2k observations, deleting one observation makes the
retained sample odd. Its median is either order statistic k or k+1 of the
original sample. The delete-one estimate therefore depends on a single central
gap g, with SE=sqrt(n−1)*g/2. If the two central order statistics tie, every
leave-one-out median is identical and the computed SE is zero.

Here both central iris values are 5.8. That explains the exact zero deletion
spread mechanically; it does not establish that a population median is known
without uncertainty. Nor does it mean that every population quantile functional
lacks differentiability: the difficulty is the local behaviour of the sample
order statistic under one deletion. Suitable delete-d inference needs estimator
regularity and appropriate growth of d with sample size. A fixed d=20 run on a
rounded, pooled sample cannot prove those asymptotic assumptions.

We preserve d=20, subset budget3000, seed7 and the bootstrap budget4000, seed1
and confidence setting0.95. The trace stores the actual sorted deletion sets and
median callbacks from the producing run. The histogram shows raw retained-130
medians; their raw variance must be multiplied by 130/20 to obtain the reported
delete-d variance. The bootstrap SE is a different conditional empirical
resampling estimate, not a truth benchmark or proof that this rescaling is
valid.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/jackknife_median.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/jackknife_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/bootstrap.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <algorithm>
#include <format>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto iris = dm::datasets::iris();
    const auto &x = iris.get_column("Sepal.Length").values();
    const auto median =
        dm::stats::jackknife_statistic(dm::stats::JackknifeStatistic::Median);
    const auto one = dm::stats::jackknife_checked(x, median);
    const auto many =
        dm::stats::jackknife_delete_d_trace(x, median, {20, 3000, 7});
    const auto boot = dm::stats::Bootstrap({4000, .95, 1}).run(x, median);
    auto sorted = x;
    std::sort(sorted.begin(), sorted.end());
    std::print("Central original values {:.1f}, {:.1f}; full median {:.1f}.\n",
               sorted.at(74), sorted.at(75), one.estimate);
    std::print("| conditional method | SE | evaluated deletion sets or bootstrap resamples | complete " "deletions |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    std::print("| delete-one median | {:.12f} | {} | true |\n",
               one.standard_error, one.leave_one_out.size());
    std::print("| delete20 median | {:.12f} | {} | {} |\n",
               many.result.standard_error, many.result.num_subsets,
               many.result.complete);
    std::print("| bootstrap median | {:.12f} | {} | false |\n",
               boot.standard_error, boot.replicates.size());
    std::print("Actual delete20 callbacks {}, raw subset population variance {:.12f}; rescaling factor " "{:.1f}.\n",
               many.evaluations, many.replicate_population_variance, 130. / 20);
    auto left =
        dm::stats::jackknife_influence_plot(x, one).title(
        "Actual delete-one medians").x_label("deleted Sepal.Length (cm)").y_label("retained-149 median (cm)").ylim(5.6, 6.1);
    auto right =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::hist(many.replicates, 12).title(
        "Actual delete20 median replicates").x_label("unscaled retained-130 median (cm)").y_label("actual subset count");
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(2, 1);
    layout.add(left).add(right).size(1000, 1000).title("Rounded iris: tied delete-one medians and sampled delete20 spread").fit_panels().save_svg("build/jackknife_median.svg");
}
```
