> Monte Carlo error and deletion-count sensitivity are different questions

When C(n,d) exceeds the budget B, the implementation samples B uniform size-d
sets with replacement across draws; an individual set never repeats an index.
With conditional subset variance v_sub and B independent ideal draws, the
population dispersion around the sampled mean has expectation (B−1)/B times
v_sub. The legacy denominator B is retained, so B=1 gives zero dispersion even
when the full deletion population varies. Its square root has additional
nonlinear Monte Carlo behaviour. Increasing B addresses this conditional
approximation, not the statistical validity of a chosen d.

The next sweep keeps the observed iris sample fixed and repeats six d values
with three seeds. Variation across seeds is conditional simulation variation,
not a confidence interval. Variation across d reflects different resampling laws
and scaling. d=1 enumerates all150 sets, so its seed is ignored; larger d values
use3000 sampled sets. The bootstrap reference uses the original 4000-resample
seed1 run again as a separate matched-input experiment.

The current original-settings delete20 SE is about0.10158 and bootstrap SE
about0.10189. The old cached0.1001 and0.1013 are not reproduced on the current
toolchain. Running the frozen original delete-d implementation and its original
median callback on this same iris sample and seed gives0.10157790660921848,
agreeing with the current result. The stored four-decimal output is historical;
comparisons here use fresh measured results without inferring the cause of that
historical difference.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/jackknife_sensitivity.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/jackknife_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/bootstrap.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <algorithm>
#include <format>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto iris = dm::datasets::iris();
    const auto &x = iris.get_column("Sepal.Length").values();
    const auto median =
        dm::stats::jackknife_statistic(dm::stats::JackknifeStatistic::Median);
    const auto boot = dm::stats::Bootstrap({4000, .95, 1}).run(x, median);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{35, 95, 210}, {210, 55, 40},
                                                {25, 150, 100}};
    std::vector<std::string> labels;
    std::size_t color = 0;
    std::print("| deleted d | seed | actual subsets | complete | median SE |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | " "---: |\n");
    for (std::uint64_t seed : {7, 19, 31}) {
        std::vector<double> ds, se;
        for (std::size_t d : {1, 5, 10, 20, 40, 80}) {
            const auto r =
                dm::stats::jackknife_delete_d(x, median, {d, 3000, seed});
            ds.push_back(double(d));
            se.push_back(r.standard_error);
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.12f} |\n", d, seed,
                       r.num_subsets, r.complete, r.standard_error);
        }
        const auto label = std::format("subset seed {}", seed);
        labels.push_back(label);
        p.line(ds, se, label, colors[color], 2).points(ds, se, label,
                                                       colors[color], 4);
        ++color;
    }
    p.abline(boot.standard_error, 0, {70, 70, 70}, 1.5).legend(labels, colors).title("Iris median: deletion-count and conditional seed sensitivity").x_label("deleted observations d").y_label("estimated median standard error (cm)").ylim(0, .15).save_svg("build/jackknife_sensitivity.svg");
    int calls = 0;
    bool budget = false, cap = false;
    const auto counted = [&](const auto &v) {
        ++calls;
        return median(v);
    };
    try {
        (void) dm::stats::jackknife_delete_d(x, counted, {20, 0, 7});
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        budget = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::stats::jackknife_delete_d_trace(x, counted, {20, 3000, 7},
                                                   {150, 62999});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        cap = true;
    }
    std::print("Zero subset budget rejected: {}. Complete63000-entry history rejected by62999 cap: {}. " "Callbacks before these admission failures: {}.\n",
               budget, cap, calls);
    if (!budget || !cap || calls != 0)
        throw std::runtime_error("admission control mismatch");
}
